{
  "source": {
    "repository": "OpenPresentation/opf-pptx",
    "commit": "6f6122cb7fb8cb89b17c1bea7981397a27ded8ed",
    "note": "toPptx default output (chartex fallback) for chartex chart types; regenerate only with an owner decision to change the default export The world-category entry (ja-JP) was regenerated for FF-49: the theme cs slot, which the Japanese language does not use, is now empty instead of repeating the latin face; the chart parts are unchanged. Regenerated for FF-62 (chart text is the preview's 12 pt, not 9 pt or the PowerPoint default, in every classic chart part): only chart-part sz values changed; commit is the base the fixture was last regenerated on. Regenerated again for the spec-gap P1 round trip (codex/spec-gaps-roundtrip, on top of FF-62): the OPF_SLIDE_V1 tag now carries the content topology of a root chart payload, so the tag parts, their relationships, content types, presentation.xml customer data and the slide custDataLst lines changed; the chart parts, embedded workbooks, theme and diagnostics are byte-identical to the FF-62 entries (verified part by part against a build of main 90802f3 before regenerating). Regenerated again for RR-11 always-on header/footer placeholders (codex/rr-11-hf-always): a deck with no footer now carries the dt/ftr/sldNum placeholders and p:hf flags on its slide master, layout and notes master; only ppt/slideMasters/slideMaster1.xml, ppt/slideLayouts/slideLayout1.xml and ppt/notesMasters/notesMaster1.xml changed (verified part by part against the previous entries); slides, charts, workbooks, theme, tags and diagnostics are byte-identical. Regenerated again for RR-29 (chartPaletteForFill, opf#270): the exported series colours come from the shared palette function, so the srgbClr values in the chart parts changed (the default light card now writes a darker fourth, fifth and later series colours where the old per-colour clamp left them within a few lightness points of their neighbours); only ppt/charts/chart*.xml differ, and with srgbClr values masked those parts are identical, verified part by part against the previous entries; slides, workbooks, theme, tags and diagnostics are byte-identical. Regenerated again for RR-36 (codex/rr-36-single-series-colour, owner-approved 2026-10-01): a single-series bar chart no longer writes a c:dPt per point, so the single-series clustered-column fallback chart parts lose their c:dPt elements; verified part by part against a build of main 4ed11db (after RR-29) with the CI-pinned core 395e4c1 (which reproduces the previous entries exactly): pareto-multi and box-multi are byte-identical, and every other deck differs only in ppt/charts/chartN.xml, which is byte-identical once the c:dPt elements are removed. Entries are toPptx(deck, {chartex: 'fallback'}) output, as test/chartex.mjs checks."
  },
